Stabwound wrote:
> Is the clan scoring going to be the same as it was last year? IE: Clan's 
> score is just a straight total of each players individual score?

The basic clan scoring function is the same, though there are 4 new 
trophies included in the calculation (though for the most part they're 
not worth many points).

> Also, in the case that a player plays 5 games in a row that qualify him for 
> both a "Hat Trick" and a "Birdie", will he get credit for both trophies for 
> his clan? I realize that this was changed late into the tournament last 
> year, and I just wanted to get it cleared up.

Any player can only receive a single trophy from the Recognition set, so 
you wouldn't get points for more than one either.  If I remember 
correctly, what was changed mid-Tournament last year was how the "with 
Bells On" modifier worked; it's currently set to double the value of the 
base trophy.

> Finally, less important but still worthy of asking: any chance of there 
> being a realtime standings page this year? :)
...

That's tricky.  Early in the Tournament, it's easy enough since it 
doesn't take long to calculate a scoreboard.  Towards the end, though, 
we had over 30k games in the database and scoreboard calculation times 
were up to over 20 minutes at one point.  We optimized the code a lot 
during the Tournament last year, and moved the control server to much 
butcher hardware this year, so it shouldn't ever get _that_ high again, 
but still ...

We'd planned to start with generating a scoreboard every 10 minutes 
(which is where we were at the end last year).  We could probably lower 
that to 5 (considering the hardware upgrade) but I'd like to hold off on 
going any lower than that till we see how the new code behaves and how 
much of a boost we get from the new hardware.

